# TalkTally — Frontend Specification

## Overview
This document describes the frontend architecture, component boundaries, key hooks, UX requirements, accessibility considerations, and testing guidance for the TalkTally mobile app.

### Purpose
Provide clear implementation guidance for mobile engineers, QA, and designers to maintain consistent behavior across screens, ensure robust voice detection, and keep the app accessible and maintainable.

## Tech Stack
- React Native 0.81.5
- Expo SDK 54
- TypeScript 5.x
- React Navigation (stack + bottom tabs)
- Zustand for state management
- Expo Audio for recording and metering
- AsyncStorage for local persistence

## Project Structure (mobile/src)
- screens/
  - LandingScreen.tsx
  - OnboardingScreen.tsx
  - HomeScreen.tsx
  - SessionScreen.tsx
  - SessionCompleteScreen.tsx
  - HistoryScreen.tsx
- navigation/
  - RootNavigator.tsx
  - MainTabs.tsx
  - types.ts
- components/
  - ErrorBoundary.tsx
  - StyledButton.tsx
  - [reusable UI components]
- hooks/
  - useVoiceDetection.ts
- features/
  - sessionData.ts
  - useSessionStore.ts
  - sessionStorage.ts
  - recommendationEngine.ts
- services/
  - logger.ts
  - analytics.ts
  - recordingService.ts
  - api.ts
- theme/
  - theme.ts

## Key Components & Responsibilities
- HomeScreen
  - Show recommendation card
  - Start/resume session
  - Display last accuracy badge and progress
- SessionScreen
  - Drive calibration, monitoring, and recording lifecycle
  - Show prompt, tip, progress bar, timer, and recording indicator
  - Handle user action (Child Responded / No Response)
  - Save recordings locally and log responses in store
- HistoryScreen
  - List past sessions, accuracy, and allow playback of local recordings
- ErrorBoundary
  - Catch rendering errors and present retry UI

## Core Hook: useVoiceDetection
Purpose: encapsulate audio setup, calibration, metering, and monitoring to expose a simple API to screens.

API surface:
- isSpeaking: boolean
- volume: number (dB)
- threshold: number (dB)
- isCalibrating: boolean
- isReady: boolean
- calibrate(): Promise<void>
- startMonitoring(): Promise<boolean>
- stopMonitoring(): Promise<void>

Behavioral Notes:
- Calibration collects samples for ~2s and sets threshold = max(-50, peakNoise + sensitivityPadding)
- Uses AudioModule.requestRecordingPermissionsAsync() for microphone permission
- Uses recorder.prepareToRecordAsync() and recorder.record(), followed by recorder.stop()
- Polls recorder.getStatus().metering every 100ms while monitoring
- Must be resilient when recorder is released/unmounted (safeGetStatus wrapper)

Performance & Battery
- Polling frequency: 100ms (balance accuracy vs CPU)
- Avoid long-running background recording; stop monitoring on unmount

## Recording Lifecycle (SessionScreen)
1. On mount: calibrate() → small delay → startMonitoring()
2. When isSpeaking transitions to true and per-step flag not set: start child recorder (prepareToRecordAsync, record)
3. On user confirming "Child Responded": stop child recorder, save file via recordingService, mark step correct
4. On "No Response" or timeout: stop/cleanup child recorder without saving
5. After final step: compile session summary and POST to backend

## Local Persistence & Sync
- sessionStorage.ts: manages AsyncStorage persistence of session history and pending uploads
- Pending sessions: queue POST requests when offline, attempt retry on network restored
- Device ID: generated once on first launch and persisted (AsyncStorage → consider SecureStore for Phase 2)

## Accessibility
- All actionable elements must have accessible labels (accessibilityLabel)
- Buttons use minimum 44x44pt touch targets
- Color contrast must meet WCAG AA for text
- Support TalkBack/VoiceOver: important text reads (prompt, mic state, timer)
- Respect reduced motion: disable pulsing animations when user prefers reduced motion

## UX & Error States
- Permission denied: show clear screen explaining why microphone required and link to settings
- Calibration failure: retry option
- No steps loaded: show a friendly error with action to return home and re-initialize
- Network failure during upload: mark session as pending; show toast & retry logic

## Testing Guidance
Unit tests
- Recommendation engine logic
- useSessionStore actions and reducers
- Audio threshold calculations (pure functions)

Integration tests
- Session flow: calibration → monitoring → detection → save → upload (mock recorder & API)
- Permissions: simulate allow/deny flows

E2E tests (on device/emulator)
- Full happy path: start session, child response, session complete
- Offline mode: start session without network and upload afterward

## Instrumentation & Logging
- Use logger.ts for structured logging; only log sensitive items in dev
- Track analytics events: session_started, session_completed, calibration_failed

## Performance Budget
- App launch: <3s cold start on mid-range device
- SessionScreen: UI must remain responsive during audio polling (avoid heavy synchronous work on JS thread)
- Keep per-frame work minimal; use native animations when possible

## Developer Experience
- Strict TypeScript settings; run tsc in CI
- ESLint + Prettier enforced in CI
- Fast reloading via Expo in development

## Future Frontend Enhancements
- Persist calibration threshold between sessions for faster startup
- Optionally export recordings for research or therapist review (user opt-in)
- Cloud backup of recordings (opt-in, encrypted)
- Theming and localization (i18n)

